  "job_B1.3.7_20251001_193224": {
    "text": "XUIII KALENDAS FEBRUARII NATALE SANCTI MAURI ABBATIS.\nMAURUS W\u00c6S GEHATEN SUM SWY\u00deE HALIG abbod, se w\u00e6s to lare bef\u00e6st sona fram iugo\u00f0e \u00feam\nHe \u00feeah wel on lare and w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e gehyrsum \u00feam halgan Benedicte on eallum his h\u00e6sum, and on\nHwilon \u00e6r we s\u00e6don on sumere o\u00f0re stowe hu se ylca Maurus, \u00feurh godes mihte eode uppon yrnendum\nOn sumne s\u00e6l eode se halga Maurus ham to mynstre weard mid his gebro\u00f0rum.\nAnd Benedictus w\u00e6s \u00fea mid anum \u00e6wf\u00e6stum were, for\u00fean \u00fee his wif w\u00e6s mid wodnysse gedreht.\nAnd Maurus \u00f0a gemette \u00e6r he to mynstre come \u00e6nne dumbne cnapan and se w\u00e6s creopere eac, ac se\nHi feollon \u00f0a butu mid flowendum tearum to Maures fotum and befengon his cneowa, halsigende \u00feurh\n\u00dea nolde Maurus \u00f0am mannum \u00fe\u00e6s ti\u00f0ian, cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t seo d\u00e6d n\u00e6re him gedafenlic o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea gebro\u00f0ra\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Maurus sona beseah to heofonum and cw\u00e6\u00fe, \u00feu ure h\u00e6lend Crist, \u00fee behete \u00feinum\n\u00c6fter \u00feisum wordum he cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00f0am wanhalan, On \u00fe\u00e6re halgan \u00f0rynnysse naman, beo \u00feu hal, cnapa,\n\u00dea aras se cnapa and up rihte eode, and mid bli\u00f0re stemne bletsode his drihten, \u00fee hine geh\u00e6lde \u00feurh\nEft \u00f0a \u00fea se halga Benedictus ham to mynstre com, and \u00fe\u00e6t wif wear\u00f0 gewittig \u00fee he fram wodnysse\nMaurus w\u00e6s eac oftost mid \u00feam eadigan Benedicte, and his wundra wiste and mid him worhte wundra.\nSume \u00fe\u00e6ra we secga\u00f0 her, sume we forsuwia\u00f0.\nAnd he w\u00e6s fyrmest muneca to \u00f0am m\u00e6ran Benedicte, and \u00fe\u00e6s mynstres geweold swa swa him\nOn \u00f0am timan asende sum ges\u00e6lig biscop of Francena rice to \u00f0am halgan f\u00e6der m\u00e6nigfealde lac and\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Benedictus be his gebro\u00f0ra r\u00e6de swa swa him God geswutolode asende \u00fea Maurum, \u00feeah \u00f0e\nHe funde him eac geferan feower o\u00f0re munecas and sume l\u00e6wede menn to \u00f0am lande mid him, and\nEft on \u00e6rnemergen sende se arwur\u00f0a Benedictus tw\u00e6gen his muneca to Maure mid lacum, \u00fe\u00e6t is mid\nIc s\u00e6cge \u00f0e to so\u00f0an \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu scealt gewitan on \u00f0am sixteo\u00f0an geare \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e \u00feu munuc wurde of \u00feisser\u00e6\nIc secge \u00fee eac nu \u00fe\u00e6t eower si\u00f0 ne bi\u00f0 na swa, swa swa we wendon, ac wyr\u00f0 elles gefadod and on\nFara\u00f0 nu gesunde and ges\u00e6lige becuma\u00f0.\nMaurus \u00f0a ferde mid mycelre blisse, and his geferan samod, to Francena rice, ac twegen his geferan\nEac hi gemetton on sumum mynstre be wege \u00e6nne blindne man se b\u00e6d his h\u00e6le georne \u00e6t \u00f0am halgan\nEft he geh\u00e6lde on o\u00f0re stowe anre wydewan sunu \u00fee unwene \u00f0a l\u00e6g, and gefrefrode \u00fea modor, and\nAnd se cnapa arn sona to Maure hrymende and cwe\u00f0ende, \u00feu ahreddest mine sawle fram fyrenum\nMaurus geseah eac swa swa him God geswutelode on \u00feam ylcan f\u00e6relde Benedictes for\u00f0si\u00f0, and hu\nHi ferdon \u00fea for\u00f0 to \u00f0am fores\u00e6dan bisceope, \u00fee hi gelangian het, ac he ne leofode na \u00fea, ac w\u00e6s for\nHi wurdon \u00fea unrote, and eoden swa \u00feeah to \u00f0am niwan bisceope, b\u00e6don his r\u00e6des, cunnodon\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he ne mihte embe munuclif \u00fea smeagen be o\u00f0res bisceopes dihte, ac wolde beon embe\nHi feordon \u00fea \u00feanon fram \u00fe\u00e6re scire bisceope, and God him foresceawode on sumere o\u00f0re scire on\nSum for\u00f0\u00feegn w\u00e6s \u00f0a welig on \u00feam lande, Florus gehaten, and se h\u00e6fde gemynt mynster to ar\u00e6renne,\nSe \u00feegn w\u00e6s wunigende butan wifes neawiste, for\u00f0an \u00fee his gebedda gefaren w\u00e6s of life, and l\u00e6fde\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Florus ferde f\u00e6gen him togeanes, and mid micelre arwur\u00f0nysse \u00fea \u00e6\u00f0elan godes menn\nSe Florus w\u00e6s \u00f0a fyrmest \u00fe\u00e6ra Francena \u00feegna, and \u00f0am cyninge leofest, \u00fee on \u00fe\u00e6ra leode rixode,\nFlorus \u00f0a cydde \u00feam cyninge his willan, and be his leafan ar\u00e6rde on his agenum lande mynster and\nHe offrode eacc \u00fea on \u00f0am ylcan dege his ancennedan sunu \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode to munuclicere\nAnd cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he sylf wolde, gif hit God swa foresceawode eall woruld\u00f0ing forl\u00e6tan, and wunian on\nHe gegaderode \u00fea swi\u00f0e gode wyrhtan gehwanon, and ar\u00e6rde \u00fe\u00e6t mynster eall be Maures r\u00e6de wi\u00f0\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a on sumum d\u00e6ge s\u00e6ton him \u00e6tg\u00e6dere Florus and Maurus to middan \u00feam wyrhtum, and\n\u00dea feol sum preost f\u00e6rlice of \u00feam weorce, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he samcucu l\u00e6g, sweltendum gelic, and fleow eall\nAc Maurus hine het beran to Martines cyrcan, and Maurus inn eode, and b\u00e6d \u00f0one \u00e6lmihtigan for his\nHe aras \u00fea eftsona and eode to \u00f0am preoste, and his wunda bletsode and cw\u00e6\u00f0 him baldlice to, On\nHe aras \u00fea gesund, swylce of sl\u00e6pe awreht and began to wundrigenne hu he wurde \u00f0ider gebroht.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se halga wer, ne wurde \u00f0u hider geferod on \u00feinum agenum fotum, ac \u00f0e feredon o\u00fere; ac\n\u00d0a eode se preost eft to his weorce, and Florus hine astrehte to Maures fotum and cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00feu eart\n\u00c6fter \u00feysum ongunnon of \u00f0am gegaderwyrhtum t\u00e6lan \u00f0one halgan \u00fee geh\u00e6lde \u00feone preost, cw\u00e6don\nAc \u00f0a \u00fea hi swi\u00feost t\u00e6ldon \u00feone so\u00f0f\u00e6stan Maurum, \u00fea wurdon afyllede mid \u00f0am fulan gaste \u00fery\nMaurus \u00fea sona mycclum wear\u00f0 astyred, and wepende eode into \u00fe\u00e6ra cyrcan, and mid mycelre\nHe eode \u00fea eft ut to \u00feam earmum wodum, and on drihtnes naman \u00fea deoflu afligde of \u00f0am wodum\nHe het eac beran into his geb\u00e6dhuse \u00fe\u00e6s for\u00f0farenan lic \u00fee se feond acwealde, and wacode ealle \u00fea\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 geendod eall \u00fe\u00e6s mynstres weorc binnan eahte gearum, and eac gehalgod mid healicum\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Florus gemunde hw\u00e6t he gemynte \u00e6t fruman, and hw\u00e6t he Gode behet \u00fea \u00f0a he began \u00fe\u00e6t\nSe cyning \u00f0a ge\u00feafode \u00feam \u00feegne his willan, \u00feeah \u00fee he unea\u00f0e mihte on his mode findan \u00fe\u00e6t he swa\n\u00c6fter \u00f0ysum ferde Florus to \u00f0am mynstre.\nAnd his kynehlaford com swa swa hi cw\u00e6don, and b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t he moste beon heora bro\u00f0or for Gode, and\nFlorus het \u00f0a for\u00f0b\u00e6ran his f\u00e6geran ma\u00f0mas on golde and on seolfre and hi Gode geoffrode, and his\nAnd se cyning blyssode and bly\u00f0e wear\u00f0 on mode, for \u00f0\u00e6s \u00feegnes gecyrrednysse and so\u00f0um geleafan.\nEft \u00e6fter gereorde, het se \u00e6\u00f0ela cyning \u00fe\u00e6t Florus hine gespr\u00e6ce \u00e6r \u00fean \u00fee he \u00feanon ferde, and he\n\u00dea weop se cyning, and \u00feancode Gode his godan wyllan, and tihte hine georne \u00fe\u00e6t he geornful w\u00e6re\nEft \u00fe\u00e6s on m\u00e6rgen rad Maurus to \u00feam lande \u00fee se cyning him geaf, and his cepte sum beddryda, se\n\u00dea bletsode Maurus \u00feone beddrydan mann, and he sona gesund sylf upp aras, swa \u00f0\u00e6t hit n\u00e6s gesene\n\u00dea bugon gehwylce \u00e6\u00f0elborenne menn to Maures mynstre to munuclicere drohtnunge.\nSume eac bef\u00e6stan heora suna him to Godes \u00feeowdome, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r gadorod w\u00e6s hund teontig\n\u00dea gecw\u00e6\u00f0 se abbod and ealle \u00fea gebro\u00f0ra \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feer ne mihte na ma muneca wunian, \u00fee l\u00e6s \u00fee \u00f0am\nHit gelamp \u00f0a si\u00f0\u00f0an \u00fe\u00e6t se ges\u00e6liga Florus gewat of worulde wuldorful to Criste, on \u00f0am \u00ferytteo\u00f0an\nSum ercediacon com eac hwilum to Maure, \u00fea n\u00e6fdon hi nan win buton on anum gewealdenan\nAnd Maurus \u00fea bletsode bli\u00f0elice \u00fe\u00e6t win, cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t God mihte gemycclian \u00feone w\u00e6tan, se \u00f0e iu on\nHi druncon \u00f0a \u00fe\u00e6t win wel hundseofontig manna, and \u00e6fre w\u00e6s se buteruc brerdful wines.\nMaurus gemette \u00e6nne man eft se w\u00e6s yfele getawod and hine \u00e6t se cancor, and his weleres w\u00e6ron\n\u00dea bletsode Maurus \u00feone mann feorran, and he sona wear\u00f0 wundorlice geh\u00e6led.\nSi\u00f0\u00f0an nolde Maurus of \u00f0am mynstre faran for nanre neode, butan he nyde sceolde, for\u00f0an \u00fee he wiste\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea gebysgod on his gebedum \u00feearle on Martines cyrcan mid his twam munecum, to \u00f0riddan\n\u00dea on sumere nihte geseah he \u00feone deofol, \u00fea \u00fea he wolde gan into Godes cyrcan.\nSe feond h\u00e6fde him mid fela o\u00f0re sceoccan, and forwyrnde him inganges, and mid graman him cw\u00e6\u00fe\nAc \u00f0u scealt witan nu \u00fe\u00e6t ic mid mislicum dea\u00f0e \u00feine munecas acwelle, swa \u00fe\u00e6t earfo\u00f0lice heora\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se halga wer to \u00f0am hetolan sceoccan, \u00f0reage \u00f0e se h\u00e6lend, \u00fee h\u00e6f\u00f0 ealles geweald, \u00feu\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a se sceocca sona fordwan of his gesih\u00f0e mid swi\u00f0licum reame, swa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a munecas micclum\nMaurus \u00f0a eode into Martines cyrcan, and mid micelre sarnysse \u00feone so\u00f0f\u00e6stan God b\u00e6d, \u00fe\u00e6t he him\nMaurus \u00f0a geseah \u00e6nne scinende engel wi\u00f0 hine standende, and \u00feas word him secgende, \u00feu Godes\nWitodlice se deofol wat towerde \u00f0ing hwilon, na symle, \u00feurh sume gebicnunge be \u00feam \u00fee he oft\n\u00c6fter \u00f0isum wordum gewat se engel him fram.\nAnd Maurus \u00fe\u00e6s on mergen \u00fea munecas gespr\u00e6c, and ealle his gesih\u00f0e him openlice s\u00e6de, and\n\u00c6fter \u00feisum wordum wurdon \u00fea munecas mycclum abryrde and heora gebeda sungon, and hi sylfe\nHim com \u00f0a se cwealm swa swa se engel gecw\u00e6\u00f0, swa \u00fe\u00e6t an hund muneca and syxtyne munecas\n\u00de\u00e6r belifon swa \u00feeah lifes on \u00f0am mynstre feower and twentig muneca \u00e6fter Maures for\u00f0si\u00f0e, and he\n\u00de\u00e6r beo\u00f0 wundra geworhte \u00f0urh \u00feone halgan wer \u00f0am \u00e6lmihtigan to lofe, se\u00f0e lyfa\u00f0 a on ecnysse.\n\u00de\u00e6s halgan Maures lif w\u00e6s \u00feus gelogod; \u00f0a \u00fea he twelf wintra w\u00e6s he w\u00e6s bet\u00e6ht Benedicte, and he\nTwegen \u00fe\u00e6ra muneca \u00f0e mid him \u00feyder comon for\u00f0ferdon \u00fe\u00e6r on \u00feam fores\u00e6dan cwealme, and\nSy wuldor and lof \u00f0am welwillendan Gode, se\u00f0e wur\u00f0a\u00f0 his halgan mid wuldre on ecnysse.\nAMEN.",
